One thing I didn't see mentioned was a closet. You know, the
door that opens onto a dead-end corridor that is one space
long. If I find one near stairs, I check to see if I have
something to stash. Elbereth on the floor and lock the door,
keeps pets and peacefuls from smudging my Elbereth and
protects from all but an incredibly unlikely sequence of
events. A container in the closet is even better. (Also a
good place to test potions).

Another problem is pets moving my stuff, or even the chest
itself. Dropping a cursed item last (on the top when you
look) will discourage a pet from moving onto the space a
prevent it from picking up anything. It will, however, dive
into the stack for it's favorite food regardless.

I would take issue with your order and reverse bags, boxes
and chests. Lighter is better if a pet moves the container
(seems to make no difference to them, just you) and lighter
is better if you want to move the stash. And when I pick one
up to make a stash, I name it STASH.

I normally use a hard gem for engraving Elbereth, beware,
however it takes one turn per letter and you can't stop once
you start, even if attacked. You can of course do it one
letter at a time if you have the patience!

